espDrop

The initial architecture and build/provisioning workflow are based on the
project conventions used by Krydix/ESPresso.

The protocol documentation is informed by public research from the Open
Wireless Link project and by inspection of the GPL-3.0 OpenDrop and OWL source
trees. No GPL implementation code is included in the MIT-licensed components.

archef2000/esp-owl is an important experimental ESP32-S3 reference. Its tree
does not currently contain a repository-level license, although individual
files carry GPL, MIT, Apache-2.0, and other notices. It is therefore kept out
of release firmware until its redistribution boundary is clarified.
